From 31ae3d8d29fefe69038220d34a3197192edf9fbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:09:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat(plugins): let plugin UIs archive or delete projects
 and sessions

Plugin tabs and tool renderers get archiveProject(path),
deleteProject(path), archiveSession(id) and deleteSession(id) on their
host API. Each makes the same request as the sidebar's archive (hidden,
restorable) or delete (with sessions and transcripts) under the
signed-in user, then cleans up local state the way the sidebar does and
refreshes it. Plugins name projects by path, which is what they know;
the host resolves the project id. Results are { ok: true } or
{ ok: false, error }, including when the request itself fails; nothing
is retried. Outside the project workspace the actions report that they
are unavailable.

The sidebar's project and session delete handlers now compare against
the selection at call time rather than the one they were created with,
so a callback held across an await, or by a plugin whose host
unmounted, cannot clear a newer selection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
